---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — AnEvergreene Studio" description="The philosophy behind AnEvergreene Studio.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">About</h1>

    <p>
      AnEvergreene Studio is a one-person operation run by Audrey Evergreene — a developer,
      writer, and maker who believes technology should feel like a deep breath, not a fire alarm.
    </p>

    <p>
      Everything here is built with the same question in mind: <em>does this respect the person
      using it?</em> That means slow transitions instead of jarring snaps. Warm colors instead
      of blinding whites. Thoughtful defaults instead of overwhelming options.
    </p>

    <h2>The philosophy</h2>

    <p>
      "Calm tech, tailored to your nervous system" isn't just a tagline — it's a design constraint.
      Every product, every service, every decision gets filtered through it. If it adds noise,
      it doesn't ship.
    </p>

    <h2>The ecosystem</h2>

    <p>
      AnEvergreene is the consciousness. Within it lives a forest of projects:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://ladyaudrey.github.io/Forest/">Forest</a></strong> — the creative
        side. Writing, art, stories, poetry. The place where things grow wild.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Studio</strong> (you're here) — the professional side. Products, services,
        and the business of making things.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="/products/">Products</a></strong> — the tools. Starting with
        <a href="/products/yournest/">YourNest</a>, with more on the way.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>

    <p>
      If any of this resonates, <a href="/contact/">reach out</a>. Whether you want a website,
      want to collaborate, or just want to say hi — the door's open.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
